{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 43, :comments ["<b>And it shall make satisfaction for its sabbaths, and they shall make satisfaction for their iniquity.</b> Corresponding to forty-nine years of a jubilee cycle in which sabbatical years were neglected, they were struck with forty-nine punishments written here in this passage. 'And they shall make satisfaction for their iniquity' — they will be appeased through the punishment that comes upon them, and they will confess and say: 'all this has come upon us because ״במשפטי מאסו״ (in My ordinances they abhorred) and ״ביען את חקותי געלה נפשם״ (because their soul abhorred My statutes).' Another interpretation: 'and they shall complete the punishment of their iniquity.' For example, if punishment befalls you in this matter — as in the case of a woman who divines by an ov."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {0 "The last example phrase 'דגבי בעלת אוב' ('as in the case of a woman who divines by an ov') is textually difficult; it appears to reference 1 Samuel 28 where the witch of En-dor is called a 'בעלת אוב', but its connection to completing a punishment is obscure. Rendered hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:15:45.220187587Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}